\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Crossed trader cash and share interventions at activation under the endogenous boundary, with $f=0.18$ and 50 seeds. In panels A to C the nine intervention cells are grouped by cash multiplier with the share multiplier on the axis, and each series is one dealer capacity. \textbf  {(A)}~Transition probability. The dashed line and band give the held-boundary value and its 95\% Wilson interval, which were identical in all nine cells because the held-boundary lattice was invariant to every intervention. \textbf  {(B)}~Median maximum drawdown on a logarithmic axis. Medians of exactly zero are drawn at the axis floor with open markers. \textbf  {(C)}~Median fraction of agent-eligible orders rejected by the dealer. \textbf  {(D)}~Transition probability against median maximum drawdown for all 27 endogenous cells, on the same logarithmic axis and with zero medians drawn as in B, with the held-boundary reference repeated.}}{13}{figure.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:balance-sheet}{{6}{13}{Crossed trader cash and share interventions at activation under the endogenous boundary, with $f=0.18$ and 50 seeds. In panels A to C the nine intervention cells are grouped by cash multiplier with the share multiplier on the axis, and each series is one dealer capacity. \textbf {(A)}~Transition probability. The dashed line and band give the held-boundary value and its 95\% Wilson interval, which were identical in all nine cells because the held-boundary lattice was invariant to every intervention. \textbf {(B)}~Median maximum drawdown on a logarithmic axis. Medians of exactly zero are drawn at the axis floor with open markers. \textbf {(C)}~Median fraction of agent-eligible orders rejected by the dealer. \textbf {(D)}~Transition probability against median maximum drawdown for all 27 endogenous cells, on the same logarithmic axis and with zero medians drawn as in B, with the held-boundary reference repeated}{figure.caption.24}{}}
